ios: renderer micro-changes with the same pixels

Three changes to the hottest renderer loops, each the same arithmetic in the same order:
- Model.render2 clears its depth buckets with one fill and scans only the depths its faces went to, instead of
  clearing and scanning the model's whole depth range (300-420 models a frame, about 240k steps). Every other depth
  below maxDepth holds no face, so the same buckets are visited in the same order.
- Pix3D.textureRaster takes u, v and w (per scanline) and their strides (per triangle) from a static Int32Array:
  7 arguments instead of 15 (curU and curV were always 0). The values are int32s either way; as arguments, those
  beyond 2^30 were boxed on every call in V8 (Chrome, Android's WebView), about 90 % of the client's garbage.
- Pix2D.cls zeroes the pixels with one native fill instead of a JS loop.

